  "url": "/ShowUserReviews-g2486879-d1063944-r751760701-Wattle_Grove_Motel-Wattle_Grove_Greater_Perth_Western_Australia.html",
  "title": "Self-quarantine heaven",
  "language": "en",
  "originalLanguage": "en",
  "roomTip": null,
  "text": "I returned to Australia on day 1 of the new laws and I am SO happy that I chose the Wattle Grove Motel for my 14 days of self-isolation.  The reason for choosing this motel was that, on their website, the rooms looked big and there is a kitchenette - a must for self-isolators.  Also, I advised the motel prior to arrival of the reason for my visit and they were warm, welcoming and very helpful towards me.\nThen I arrived - and the staff were kind, sympathetic, professional and positive towards me.  I was VERY surprised to discover that they had robust procedures in place for my visit including self-quarantine signage on my door (as a courtesy to other guests), a fact sheet regarding the virus and a specific motel fact sheet on exactly how they would deal with my presence at the motel.  They were thorough and reassuring while being strict and professional, and even checked in with me each day to check on my mental health.   I can't speak more highly of this motel.\nIn addition, they offer continental breakfast and nightly dinner specials (at VERY reasonable prices).\nI will forever be indebted to the Wattle Grove Motel for their hospitality during this difficult time and well after this crisis is over I will remain a loyal customer.",
